Subject: [PATCH 11297/11362] [outer-loop] Substrate census: split blocked runs
 out of "unfloored"; record corrections

Found by checking my own note against the sweep before the reviewer did.

- The gate's floor function returns None for any `blocked_*` verdict (its first
  branch). So "751 draw no floor" mixed two populations: 251 blocked runs, where
  no floor is the design, and 500 ignored declarations. The census now reports
  `precondition_blocked` and the effective class `blocked_no_run`.
- The 16 `verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates` misses are exact strings:
  13 blocked runs, 3 with typed live evidence. The note had blamed a trailing
  note. Wrong; corrected in place and listed in the note's new section 10.
- Appendix B backfill count 1028 -> 965 (cross-tab, not summed populations).
- "17 floor reasons" -> 16; "eight further reasons" -> six.

Tests: 7 (fixture gains a blocked artifact). Mutation M6 (blocked detection
deleted at the call site) RED on 2 tests, restored byte-identically, GREEN.
Ran unlocked; PYTHONPATH pinned to this worktree.

Also recorded: `eval-run-consumer-field-lint` refuses every scripts/*.py commit
from a worktree or fresh clone because `results/arc_leaderboard_eval_runs` is
untracked and the hook does not pass `--runs-dir`. Known-issues entry added;
a temporary read-only symlink was used for this session's commits.

